    <node id="ANOKI">
      <data key="d0">ANIMAL</data>
      <data key="d1">ANOKI is a polar bear who moved to Seneca Park Zoo in 2018 and is known for her curiosity and fondness for yams and peanut butter. She is involved in blood draw training and has a detailed travel and life history. ANOKI is also part of a study about the importance of land-based, human-provisioned foods and is mentioned in association with Dr. Karyn Rode in the context of polar bear research.</data>
      <data key="d2">14d429568463adbb525417ad6aa15254,1f71ca11e0da3f8a8a1776a16fd724c3,55e333329ce5a8bb7e63f67578138cd3,937ae63cfd0860b674756ae48deb18d1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ZOO EXHIBIT">
      <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Location where the sign about Anoki is mounted, and where she likely resides</data>
      <data key="d2">1f71ca11e0da3f8a8a1776a16fd724c3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CALIFORNIA SEA LION">
      <data key="d0">ANIMAL</data>
      <data key="d1">The California sea lion is a protected marine mammal species residing along the Pacific west coast of North America. Known for its speed and distinctive diet, this species often interacts with fisheries, which has highlighted its ecological importance. The California sea lion is also featured in outdoor exhibits, where informative signs provide educational insights into its behavior and habitat.</data>
      <data key="d2">1f71ca11e0da3f8a8a1776a16fd724c3,da288d535b2debcfbed9d301b921a7cd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SEA LION EXHIBIT">
      <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Outdoor exhibit featuring a rocky habitat with water, suitable for California sea lions</data>
      <data key="d2">1f71ca11e0da3f8a8a1776a16fd724c3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PENGUINS">
      <data key="d0">ANIMAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Penguins at Seneca Park Zoo are charming birds that captivate human observers with their typical behaviors. These animals, whose debut and activities are announced by the zoo, are observed engaging in various activities within their enclosure, enjoying their time and providing an enchanting experience for visitors.</data>
      <data key="d2">1f71ca11e0da3f8a8a1776a16fd724c3,807d66922b9b185cfc13dde4cefa5199,e343b6fc4fc15c701802319fca7f2111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PENGUIN ENCLOSURE">
      <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Enclosure filled with penguins, observed by a person through glass</data>
      <data key="d2">1f71ca11e0da3f8a8a1776a16fd724c3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AQUATIC ANIMAL ENCLOSURE">
      <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
      <data key="d1">An enclosure with clear water and large rocks, surrounded by lush greenery, hinting at a habitat for aquatic animals</data>
      <data key="d2">1f71ca11e0da3f8a8a1776a16fd724c3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INFORMATIVE SIGN">
      <data key="d0">OBJECT</data>
      <data key="d1">The informative signs are strategically placed at various exhibits to educate visitors about different animals. One sign provides details about Anoki, the polar bear, and another sign offers information about the California Sea Lion, each located at their respective exhibits. Additionally, there is a sign that provides information about the Sandhill Crane, which is adorned with images and a map, and is situated in a woodland setting. These signs serve as educational tools to enhance visitor understanding of the animals' habitats and characteristics.</data>
      <data key="d2">1f71ca11e0da3f8a8a1776a16fd724c3,8edfdc2d2553c09aedca682d282d9365,a5a30283cdfa684c563779f3704abc58,b4d2cc3abe1f734c12be104f7160649b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INDIVIDUAL">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">The "INDIVIDUAL" entity refers to a membership type at the zoo specifically designed for individual members. Additionally, it is an award category that does not have an age restriction and focuses on recognizing innovative solutions to environmental issues.</data>
      <data key="d2">1f71ca11e0da3f8a8a1776a16fd724c3,30c61f2e8eb9ec787335dd5146b1dcd3,e55b1327e026128f213265c2470cb046</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COFFEE CUP">
      <data key="d0">OBJECT</data>
      <data key="d1">A forgotten item on a wooden post inside the penguin enclosure, adding a quirky element to the scene</data>
      <data key="d2">e343b6fc4fc15c701802319fca7f2111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DAYTIME">
      <data key="d0">TIME</data>
      <data key="d1">The lighting in the scene suggests it is daytime, with natural light illuminating the enclosure</data>
      <data key="d2">e343b6fc4fc15c701802319fca7f2111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INFORMATIVE SIGN ABOUT PENGUINS">
      <data key="d0">OBJECT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sign mounted outdoors, providing educational information about penguins, their challenges, and declining populations</data>
      <data key="d2">e343b6fc4fc15c701802319fca7f2111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TOTEM POLE SIGN">
      <data key="d0">OBJECT</data>
      <data key="d1">An informative sign, flipped upside down, explaining the cultural significance and history of totem poles</data>
      <data key="d2">e343b6fc4fc15c701802319fca7f2111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NATIVE AMERICAN MAN">
      <data key="d0">HUMAN</data>
