      <data key="d2">e343b6fc4fc15c701802319fca7f2111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GITXSAN VILLAGE">
      <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
      <data key="d1">A village depicted in a photo on the totem pole sign, showing a snowy scene with tall totem poles</data>
      <data key="d2">e343b6fc4fc15c701802319fca7f2111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TOTEM POLE">
      <data key="d0">OBJECT</data>
      <data key="d1">The totem pole, crafted by Native American artists, is a towering and intricately carved structure located in a serene forest setting. It features a variety of symbols, including an eagle, a box with the sun and moon, a depiction of a woman, and a beaver chewing a twig. Each of these symbols holds cultural and historical significance, representing various aspects of Native American heritage and storytelling.</data>
      <data key="d2">17c0689c47bb3c47d7e7005247ee72b3,b4d2cc3abe1f734c12be104f7160649b,e343b6fc4fc15c701802319fca7f2111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GLASS">
      <data key="d0">OBJECT</data>
      <data key="d1">Material through which the person is seen taking a picture or video of the penguins</data>
      <data key="d2">e343b6fc4fc15c701802319fca7f2111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WOODEN STRUCTURE">
      <data key="d0">OBJECT</data>
      <data key="d1">The wooden structure is a rustic construction that resembles an old log cabin or frontier fort. Additionally, it serves a functional purpose as the structure on which an informative sign about penguins is mounted.</data>
      <data key="d2">1bf82145f059fdc9615e35813e98e2af,e343b6fc4fc15c701802319fca7f2111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ZOO OR NATURE RESERVE">
      <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Possible location where the informative sign about penguins is placed, suggesting an outdoor educational setting</data>
      <data key="d2">e343b6fc4fc15c701802319fca7f2111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUN">
      <data key="d0">NATURAL PHENOMENON</data>
      <data key="d1">The sun, shining brightly and likely indicating it is midday, serves as the primary source of natural light and casts sharp shadows in the scene described. It is also mentioned in relation to Pimento, who enjoys relaxing in the sun during her retirement. This scene includes an informative sign about penguins, suggesting the setting may be an outdoor area possibly related to wildlife or a conservation space.</data>
      <data key="d2">4fdb8dedb8854ac8f2c3684c3fb89524,7f9a74e3a14e39a9d1c84fe7b4cff52c,e343b6fc4fc15c701802319fca7f2111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NATIVE AMERICAN ARTISTS">
      <data key="d0">GROUP</data>
      <data key="d1">Native American artists, specifically from the Northwest Coast of North America, are recognized for their creation of totem poles, as indicated on the totem pole sign. These artists are celebrated for their contributions to this traditional art form.</data>
      <data key="d2">17c0689c47bb3c47d7e7005247ee72b3,e343b6fc4fc15c701802319fca7f2111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANIMALS, SPIRITS, AND BELIEFS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Themes depicted on totem poles as mentioned on the totem pole sign</data>
      <data key="d2">e343b6fc4fc15c701802319fca7f2111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PHOTO OF NATIVE AMERICAN MAN">
      <data key="d0">OBJECT</data>
      <data key="d1">Image on the totem pole sign showing a Native American man carving a totem pole</data>
      <data key="d2">e343b6fc4fc15c701802319fca7f2111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PHOTO OF GITXSAN VILLAGE">
      <data key="d0">OBJECT</data>
      <data key="d1">Image on the totem pole sign showing the snowy entrance to Gitxsan Village</data>
      <data key="d2">e343b6fc4fc15c701802319fca7f2111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SERENE FOREST SETTING">
      <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Location surrounding the totem pole, characterized by lush greenery and peaceful atmosphere</data>
      <data key="d2">e343b6fc4fc15c701802319fca7f2111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WOODEN INFORMATION BOARD">
      <data key="d0">OBJECT</data>
      <data key="d1">Board near the totem pole providing information about its cultural significance</data>
      <data key="d2">e343b6fc4fc15c701802319fca7f2111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WOODEN POST">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1">The "WOODEN POST" is a structure made of wood, primarily utilized to support signs, such as the 'Animal Hospital' sign.</data>
      <data key="d2">8910b045a5c0843c336e9ebc84c072ec,e343b6fc4fc15c701802319fca7f2111</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EAGLE">
      <data key="d0">SYMBOL, ANIMAL</data>
      <data key="d1">The eagle is prominently featured as a symbol of freedom on a totem pole, which is significant to the community of Rochester. It is associated with the artists' clan, emphasizing its cultural and symbolic importance in representing liberty for the residents of the area.</data>
      <data key="d2">17c0689c47bb3c47d7e7005247ee72b3,b4d2cc3abe1f734c12be104f7160649b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BOX WITH THE SUN AND MOON">
      <data key="d0">SYMBOL, ARTIFACT</data>
      <data key="d1">Symbol on the totem pole narrating a story about ancient light capturing techniques</data>
      <data key="d2">b4d2cc3abe1f734c12be104f7160649b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WOMAN">
      <data key="d0">SYMBOL, HISTORICAL FIGURE</data>
      <data key="d1">The totem pole features a depiction of a woman that honors strong historical figures and celebrates the Bear Mother, alongside notable women such as Susan B. Anthony and Harriet Tubman. This symbol on the totem pole serves to recognize and honor the contributions and strength of women in general.</data>
      <data key="d2">17c0689c47bb3c47d7e7005247ee72b3,b4d2cc3abe1f734c12be104f7160649b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BEAVER CHEWING A TWIG">
      <data key="d0">SYMBOL, ANIMAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Symbol on the totem pole representing hard work and determination, honoring the industrious nature of beavers</data>
      <data key="d2">b4d2cc3abe1f734c12be104f7160649b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CRANE">
      <data key="d0">ANIMAL, BIRD</data>
      <data key="d1">A bird resembling a crane or heron, captured in a serene nature-filled scene</data>
      <data key="d2">b4d2cc3abe1f734c12be104f7160649b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GIRAFFES">
      <data key="d0">ANIMAL, SPECIES</data>
      <data key="d1">Giraffes are depicted as majestic creatures that are content in their environment, potentially serving as the main attraction in the scene. They are also featured on an informative signboard that discusses their conservation and the shifts in their population, highlighting the importance of their preservation.</data>
