    <node id="AFRICAN ELEPHANT">
      <data key="d0">ANIMAL</data>
      <data key="d1">The African Elephant is a large herbivorous mammal native to Africa, prominently featured in the zoo's collection. It is often found in open forests and grasslands and is known for taking center stage in zoo settings, where it likely enjoys mud baths. This species is highlighted in the document under the 'More Animals From Africa' section and is recognized as being threatened by the ivory trade and habitat destruction. The African Elephant is repeatedly mentioned as a significant part of the zoo's array of animals from Africa.</data>
