    <node id="AMUR TIGER">
      <data key="d0">ANIMAL, ENDANGERED SPECIES</data>
      <data key="d1">The Amur Tiger, whose death was recently announced at Seneca Park Zoo, is an animal known for its distinct habitat, size, and conservation status, details of which are displayed on a zoo sign. This species is significant in the context of wildlife conservation and environmental awareness.</data>
      <data key="d2">17c0689c47bb3c47d7e7005247ee72b3,807d66922b9b185cfc13dde4cefa5199,d929c89af727d93966fdfa5f843ed8c6,f4b84d8469e84e31e4d8c0f2241ebb94</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GRAY WOLF">
      <data key="d0">ANIMAL</data>
      <data key="d1">The Gray Wolf is a magnificent mammal species observed in a natural setting during midday. It is listed under the 'More Animals from North America' section in a document and also featured on a zoo sign, which provides detailed information about its scientific name, diet, social structure, and conservation status.</data>
      <data key="d2">17c0689c47bb3c47d7e7005247ee72b3,360b21cff28e96518b1080330f37b4f1,a5a30283cdfa684c563779f3704abc58,b2d180d00dbf4721b8ae9121fe3bd2b5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SNOW LEOPARD">
      <data key="d0">ANIMAL</data>
      <data key="d1">The Snow Leopard, scientifically known as Panthera uncia, is a rare and elusive big cat found in the high, rugged mountains of Central Asia. It faces threats such as poaching and habitat loss. This animal is featured on an informative sign in a zoo or wildlife sanctuary, indicating its presence and providing educational information about its characteristics and conservation status. Recently, the arrival of a Snow Leopard at Seneca Park Zoo was announced, highlighting its significance as a notable addition to the zoo's collection of animals from Asia, as documented in various texts and lists.</data>
      <data key="d2">17c0689c47bb3c47d7e7005247ee72b3,6d14ad0fec20f957fa86ed5bba9c5842,807d66922b9b185cfc13dde4cefa5199,a5a30283cdfa684c563779f3704abc58,d929c89af727d93966fdfa5f843ed8c6,f4b84d8469e84e31e4d8c0f2241ebb94</data>
    </node>
