    <node id="RED PANDA">
      <data key="d0">ANIMAL</data>
      <data key="d1">The Red Panda is an arboreal species primarily found throughout the Himalayan Mountains. It is primarily herbivorous and faces significant threats such as deforestation and poaching. This endangered species has a declining population due to habitat loss among other factors. The Red Panda is listed as one of the animals from Asia and is a crowd favorite, prominently featured on signs and banners at the zoo entrance. It is also potentially present at the zoo, as mentioned in the text.</data>
      <data key="d2">191f7e3587b17342ccf913b6c3d77933,6d14ad0fec20f957fa86ed5bba9c5842,a5a30283cdfa684c563779f3704abc58,d929c89af727d93966fdfa5f843ed8c6,f4b84d8469e84e31e4d8c0f2241ebb94</data>
    </node>
