      <data key="d2">a5a30283cdfa684c563779f3704abc58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CENTER FOR BIODIVERSITY EXPLORATION">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Center for Biodiversity Exploration is an organization dedicated to exploring and educating about biodiversity. It features a vibrant sign and large blue double doors, creating an inviting and educational atmosphere. The center enforces specific rules such as 'No Food or Drink' to maintain its environment. It is frequently mentioned in relation to various creatures, highlighting its role in biodiversity education.</data>
      <data key="d2">19fd40a0ecae55e9d92fa6c64b312c42,a5a30283cdfa684c563779f3704abc58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INFORMATIVE POSTER">
      <data key="d0">OBJECT</data>
      <data key="d1">A poster providing details about the plight of red pandas, mounted on a rustic wooden wall</data>
      <data key="d2">a5a30283cdfa684c563779f3704abc58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DISPLAY">
      <data key="d0">OBJECT</data>
      <data key="d1">An informative display about snow leopards, providing educational information and conservation messages</data>
      <data key="d2">a5a30283cdfa684c563779f3704abc58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LAKE STURGEON">
      <data key="d0">ANIMAL, SPECIES</data>
      <data key="d1">The Lake Sturgeon is a fish species known for its long lifespan and large size. It is native to North America and has been the focus of extensive conservation efforts, particularly in the Genesee River area. These efforts, which have been ongoing for twenty years and involve multiple organizations, aim to restore the population of this indigenous species, which was on the brink of extinction. The Lake Sturgeon is featured in educational programs and signs surrounded by lush greenery to raise public awareness. It is also listed under the 'More Animals from North America' section in a document, indicating its significance and presence, potentially at a zoo.</data>
      <data key="d2">19fd40a0ecae55e9d92fa6c64b312c42,360b21cff28e96518b1080330f37b4f1,45d8d5e706be27731202735287418cab,532641424d1ac585278bb60c24a09a1c,6d14ad0fec20f957fa86ed5bba9c5842,b2d180d00dbf4721b8ae9121fe3bd2b5,b444a72d50d13af97d816c1ebde75f41</data>
    </node>
