      <data key="d2">6f62d2860d0f3958caa46b6051845518</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MILESTONE CELEBRATIONS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT, SERVICE</data>
      <data key="d1">A type of private event hosted at Seneca Park Zoo focusing on family events like birthdays and reunions"</data>
      <data key="d2">6f62d2860d0f3958caa46b6051845518</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COMPANY OUTINGS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT, SERVICE</data>
      <data key="d1">Company outings at Seneca Park Zoo are special private events designed specifically for companies looking to provide a fun and enriching experience for their employees and their families. These outings include interactive and educational activities that focus on engagement and enjoyment for all attendees.</data>
      <data key="d2">30c61f2e8eb9ec787335dd5146b1dcd3,6f62d2860d0f3958caa46b6051845518</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FEEDING ZOO ANIMALS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT, EXPERIENCE</data>
      <data key="d1">An experience at Seneca Park Zoo where guests can feed various zoo animals</data>
      <data key="d2">6f62d2860d0f3958caa46b6051845518</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WHITE RHINO">
      <data key="d0">ANIMAL</data>
      <data key="d1">The White Rhino, known for its squared lip adapted to grazing in African grasslands, is a resident animal at the zoo, specifically located in the Animals of the Savanna building. This species is part of the Species Survival Plan committee considerations for placement in facilities based on various factors. At Seneca Park Zoo, the White Rhino, referred to as Jiwe, is featured in the Rhino Encounter where guests can learn about and touch the animal. It is listed as one of the animals from Africa and is included in the 'More Animals From Africa' section in the zoo's documentation.</data>
      <data key="d2">02ed48373f13fe54d7540874b5d52187,0e82357242396a0c25a818c5edb5e69d,2aff8b93e799e360f021a8d30f349244,5b32cc9af4441f9451a68576d6befb8c,6d14ad0fec20f957fa86ed5bba9c5842,6f62d2860d0f3958caa46b6051845518,93b8cec1c161812c432a361ca9f5e110,fdad927a279adcc084120bd45b615091</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MASAI GIRAFFES">
      <data key="d0">ANIMAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Masai giraffes are a species of giraffes that guests can interact with at Seneca Park Zoo through feeding encounters. These encounters occur during the Giraffe Feedings event, providing visitors with a unique opportunity to engage closely with these majestic animals.</data>
      <data key="d2">2aff8b93e799e360f021a8d30f349244,6f62d2860d0f3958caa46b6051845518,93b8cec1c161812c432a361ca9f5e110</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AFRICAN ELEPHANTS">
      <data key="d0">ANIMAL</data>
      <data key="d1">African elephants at Seneca Park Zoo are a species that guests can interact with during the Elephant Encounter. These elephants are also used for testing equipment such as radio telemetry devices. This interaction allows visitors to learn more about African elephants while providing an opportunity for the zoo to conduct important research and testing.</data>
      <data key="d2">012abaca5ac0051ac1d5f45b5ef82a3d,2aff8b93e799e360f021a8d30f349244,2c20259c06c872b8077b598161f55f87,6f62d2860d0f3958caa46b6051845518</data>
    </node>
    <node id="KEEPER CHATS">
      <data key="d0" />
      <data key="d1" />
      <data key="d2">6f62d2860d0f3958caa46b6051845518</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRIVATE EVENT SPACES AND VENUES">
      <data key="d0">SECTION</data>
      <data key="d1">Section in the document that lists different venues available for private events at the zoo</data>
      <data key="d2">30c61f2e8eb9ec787335dd5146b1dcd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EAGLE&#8217;S LANDING PAVILION">
      <data key="d0">VENUE</data>
      <data key="d1">Eagle&#8217;s Landing Pavilion is a large timber frame pavilion located within the zoo, equipped with lights, fans, and heaters to ensure guest comfort. It serves as the venue for performances of the musical piece 'Carnival of the Animals'.</data>
      <data key="d2">30c61f2e8eb9ec787335dd5146b1dcd3,e3c5b5a66202ce1617b0ce83eb744e23</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ROCKY COASTS GALLERY">
      <data key="d0">VENUE</data>
      <data key="d1">A venue at the zoo offering underwater viewing of polar bears and sea lions</data>
      <data key="d2">30c61f2e8eb9ec787335dd5146b1dcd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SAVANNA PLAZA">
      <data key="d0">VENUE</data>
      <data key="d1">An open-air venue at the zoo for cocktail parties with views of giraffes and zebras</data>
      <data key="d2">30c61f2e8eb9ec787335dd5146b1dcd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BABOON CAMP PLAZA">
      <data key="d0">VENUE</data>
      <data key="d1">A venue at the zoo located in 'A Step Into Africa' for dining by the baboons and viewing lions</data>
      <data key="d2">30c61f2e8eb9ec787335dd5146b1dcd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MAIN EVENT TENT">
      <data key="d0">VENUE</data>
      <data key="d1">An outdoor tent at the zoo for picnics, reunions, and parties, located between the Amur tiger and African penguins</data>
      <data key="d2">30c61f2e8eb9ec787335dd5146b1dcd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ZOO MEMBERSHIP">
      <data key="d0">PROGRAM</data>
      <data key="d1">Membership program at the zoo that supports global conservation efforts and offers various benefits</data>
      <data key="d2">30c61f2e8eb9ec787335dd5146b1dcd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CONSERVATION EFFORTS">
      <data key="d0">INITIATIVE</data>
      <data key="d1">Conservation efforts encompass a range of activities aimed at preserving wildlife and natural habitats. These efforts include supporting organizations such as Lion Landscapes and programs like African Lion SAFE. Additionally, conservation efforts are integral to the zoo's mission, focusing on wildlife conservation both locally and globally. The zoo supports these efforts through various membership programs and is actively planning future activities to preserve biodiversity and ecosystems, drawing insights from experiences such as the Ivohiboro trip.</data>
      <data key="d2">012abaca5ac0051ac1d5f45b5ef82a3d,30c61f2e8eb9ec787335dd5146b1dcd3,4f0216fbf293d41283768fcf5c6a176f,b0b9a7e2f9c8c13b352787d0d7c78fe6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MEMBERSHIP PACKAGES">
      <data key="d0">SECTION</data>
      <data key="d1">Section in the document detailing different membership packages available at the zoo</data>
      <data key="d2">30c61f2e8eb9ec787335dd5146b1dcd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COLLEGE STUDENT">
      <data key="d0">MEMBERSHIP TYPE</data>
      <data key="d1">A membership type at the zoo specifically for college students, requiring student ID for entry</data>
      <data key="d2">30c61f2e8eb9ec787335dd5146b1dcd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COUPLE">
      <data key="d0">MEMBERSHIP TYPE</data>
