    <node id="MONARCH BUTTERFLY">
      <data key="d0">SPECIES</data>
      <data key="d1">The Monarch Butterfly is a species that has been the focus of conservation efforts, particularly through the Butterfly Beltway programs. Since 2002, the zoo has also been involved in conserving pollinator sites specifically for this species. These initiatives highlight the importance of the Monarch Butterfly in biodiversity and the efforts being made to preserve its habitat.</data>
      <data key="d2">37c417e9fb3db505eeeaa12d3f028e77,b444a72d50d13af97d816c1ebde75f41,f7d18cffd13aa901313d3d4fceef2575</data>
