    <node id="SAFE">
      <data key="d0">PROGRAM</data>
      <data key="d1">A program that combines the power of zoo and aquarium visitors with the expertise of AZA members and partners to save vulnerable wildlife species from extinction</data>
      <data key="d2">9b7c814666ecc42fbf1a45118e7f2977</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AFRICAN LION">
      <data key="d0">ANIMAL</data>
      <data key="d1">The African Lion is a big cat species native to Africa and is part of the zoo's collection. It is specifically mentioned in the document as one of the animals from Africa and is listed in the 'More Animals From Africa' section. This species of lion, which arrived at the zoo from South Africa, is part of the Species Survival Plan and is designated as one of the SAFE species at the zoo. The African Lion faces threats such as human conflict and habitat loss.</data>
      <data key="d2">02ed48373f13fe54d7540874b5d52187,0e82357242396a0c25a818c5edb5e69d,0fc43ac1990ac497fc8887d975c38133,5b32cc9af4441f9451a68576d6befb8c,8a4ff50d66bebd669f478e706f701304,9b7c814666ecc42fbf1a45118e7f2977,fdad927a279adcc084120bd45b615091</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AFRICAN PENGUIN">
      <data key="d0">ANIMAL</data>
      <data key="d1">The African Penguin is a species native to Africa and is part of the zoo's collection. It is mentioned in the document as one of the animals from Africa and is specifically listed in the 'More Animals From Africa' section. Additionally, it is recognized as one of the SAFE (Saving Animals From Extinction) species at the zoo, highlighting its conservation importance. The document provides a detailed description of the living conditions and care of African Penguins within the zoo environment.</data>
      <data key="d2">0e82357242396a0c25a818c5edb5e69d,0fc43ac1990ac497fc8887d975c38133,5b32cc9af4441f9451a68576d6befb8c,8a4ff50d66bebd669f478e706f701304,9b7c814666ecc42fbf1a45118e7f2977,fdad927a279adcc084120bd45b615091</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MASAI GIRAFFE">
      <data key="d0">ANIMAL</data>
      <data key="d1">The Masai giraffe is a subspecies of giraffe native to Africa and is part of the collection at Seneca Park Zoo. This species is housed north of the elephant barn and is involved in various events at the zoo, including notable births and a death. The Masai giraffe is specifically detailed in the zoo's documentation, where individual giraffes are named and their birth details are provided. It is listed as one of the animals from Africa and is also mentioned in the 'More Animals From Africa' section of the document. Additionally, the Masai giraffe is recognized as one of the SAFE species at the zoo, indicating its significance in conservation efforts.</data>
      <data key="d2">02ed48373f13fe54d7540874b5d52187,0e82357242396a0c25a818c5edb5e69d,0fc43ac1990ac497fc8887d975c38133,3a13fc10eb422fca000ef83965be7c54,5b32cc9af4441f9451a68576d6befb8c,6d14ad0fec20f957fa86ed5bba9c5842,8a4ff50d66bebd669f478e706f701304,9b7c814666ecc42fbf1a45118e7f2977,fdad927a279adcc084120bd45b615091</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SCIENTIFIC RESEARCH">
      <data key="d0">ACTIVITY</data>
      <data key="d1">Research activities at the zoo involving wildlife biologists, nutritionists, and other specialists to save threatened and endangered wildlife</data>
      <data key="d2">9b7c814666ecc42fbf1a45118e7f2977</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BABOON COGNITIVE STUDIES">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH PROJECT</data>
      <data key="d1">A research initiative led by University of Rochester scientists to evaluate learning abilities and thought processes of Olive baboons at the zoo</data>
      <data key="d2">9b7c814666ecc42fbf1a45118e7f2977</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UNIVERSITY OF ROCHESTER">
      <data key="d0">INSTITUTION</data>
      <data key="d1">The University of Rochester is actively involved in scientific research through collaborations with the zoo, specifically leading the Baboon Cognitive Studies. This partnership highlights the university's commitment to advancing knowledge in animal behavior and cognition.</data>
      <data key="d2">9b7c814666ecc42fbf1a45118e7f2977,b444a72d50d13af97d816c1ebde75f41</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DR. JESSICA CANTLON">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Assistant Professor leading the Baboon Cognitive Studies at the zoo</data>
