    <node id="IUCN RED LIST">
      <data key="d0">CONSERVATION STATUS</data>
      <data key="d1">The IUCN Red List, provided by the International Union for Conservation of Nature, is a critical conservation status listing used globally to assess the extinction risk of various wildlife species. This list classifies species based on their conservation status and includes animals such as the snow leopard, red panda, African elephant, white rhino, and African lion. It serves as a comprehensive tool to measure and communicate the urgency of wildlife conservation efforts and the potential threats to biodiversity.</data>
      <data key="d2">02ed48373f13fe54d7540874b5d52187,48f339f528142c5c993c7020c8b79320,5b32cc9af4441f9451a68576d6befb8c,8a4ff50d66bebd669f478e706f701304,b2d180d00dbf4721b8ae9121fe3bd2b5,d929c89af727d93966fdfa5f843ed8c6,f4b84d8469e84e31e4d8c0f2241ebb94</data>
    </node>
