    <node id="MADAGASCAR HISSING COCKROACH">
      <data key="d0">ANIMAL</data>
      <data key="d1">The Madagascar hissing cockroach is a species of cockroach that is native to Madagascar and plays a crucial role as a decomposer in the ecosystem. It is mentioned in various contexts including a list of animals from Africa, and specifically highlighted in the 'More Animals From Africa' section. Additionally, it is noted as one of the animals potentially present at the zoo. This species is recognized for its distinct presence both geographically and within community structures where it contributes to ecological balance.</data>
