    <node id="MADAGASCAR TREE BOA">
      <data key="d0">ANIMAL</data>
      <data key="d1">The Madagascar Tree Boa is a species of boa that is native to Madagascar and nearby islands. It is known for feeding on birds, bats, and small mammals. This snake is frequently mentioned in various contexts related to African wildlife, including being listed in documents and texts as one of the animals from Africa. Additionally, it is potentially present in zoos and is specifically mentioned in the 'More Animals From Africa' section of a document.</data>
