      <data key="d0">ANIMAL</data>
      <data key="d1">The Naked Mole Rat, a species of rodent native to East Africa, is housed in the new Animals of the Savanna building at Seneca Park Zoo. This species primarily feeds on tubers and lives in underground tunnels. It is mentioned in various sections of the document, including as part of the zoo's collection and specifically in the 'More Animals From Africa' section, indicating its presence at the zoo and highlighting its African origin.</data>
