      <data key="d1">"SCIENCE SAVING SPECIES" is a program at Seneca Park Zoo dedicated to species conservation through scientific research and collaboration with various institutions. This initiative focuses on advancing the understanding of animal biology and employs scientific approaches to prevent various species from extinction. The program is highlighted in news items for its efforts in conservation and its role in fostering partnerships that enhance research and conservation strategies.</data>
