    <node id="INTERNATIONAL UNION FOR CONSERVATION OF NATURE (IUCN)">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The International Union for Conservation of Nature (IUCN) is an international organization that provides the conservation status of wildlife species, including the Red List status, which assesses the extinction risk of species.</data>
      <data key="d2">0fc43ac1990ac497fc8887d975c38133,da288d535b2debcfbed9d301b921a7cd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CANADA LYNX">
      <data key="d0">ANIMAL</data>
      <data key="d1">The Canada Lynx is a mammal species native to North America, specifically listed under the section 'More Animals from North America' in various documents. This species of lynx is recognized as threatened in some regions and is subject to various conservation measures to protect its population and habitat.</data>
      <data key="d2">360b21cff28e96518b1080330f37b4f1,b2d180d00dbf4721b8ae9121fe3bd2b5,da288d535b2debcfbed9d301b921a7cd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BIANCA">
      <data key="d0">ANIMAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Bianca is a female Canadian lynx residing at the Zoo, born in 2013. She is known for her curious nature and is the mother to Stanley. Bianca is the subject of various enrichment activities at the zoo, which cater to her inquisitive behavior.</data>
      <data key="d2">3b1f9ee615cb8af34064946e8bbc5653,da288d535b2debcfbed9d301b921a7cd</data>
    </node>
