    <edge source="MARINE BIRDS OF THE AMERICAS" target="SEA MCKEON">
      <data key="d4">28.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Sea McKeon is the designated speaker at the Marine Birds of the Americas event.</data>
      <data key="d6">25244450e63663bca5ac126d6ed1c735,37145c80bbad9e7bb1716a1e0492645e,9fbeec723e4f071989819b22d7317dc6</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MARINE BIRDS OF THE AMERICAS" target="ROCHESTER BIRDING ASSOCIATION">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The Rochester Birding Association is a partner for the Marine Birds of the Americas event</data>
      <data key="d6">25244450e63663bca5ac126d6ed1c735</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MARINE BIRDS OF THE AMERICAS" target="AMERICAN BIRD CONSERVANCY">
      <data key="d4">26.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The "Marine Birds of the Americas" event features discussions on marine birds and their conservation, with a focus on the efforts of the American Bird Conservancy. Sea McKeon represents the American Bird Conservancy at this event, highlighting the organization's role in marine bird conservation. This gathering serves as a platform for sharing knowledge and strategies related to the preservation of marine bird species across the Americas.</data>
      <data key="d6">1e20e07194c6b756df1b77ab0d6b272b,25244450e63663bca5ac126d6ed1c735,37145c80bbad9e7bb1716a1e0492645e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MARINE BIRDS OF THE AMERICAS" target="RANDI MINETOR">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Randi Minetor is actively engaged in events focused on environmental and wildlife topics. She participates in a discussion event titled "Marine Birds of the Americas" and is also involved in a conversation event with Sea McKeon. These involvements highlight her interest and dedication to the study and conservation of marine birds in the Americas.</data>
      <data key="d6">37145c80bbad9e7bb1716a1e0492645e,9fbeec723e4f071989819b22d7317dc6</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MARINE BIRDS OF THE AMERICAS" target="MCKEON">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">McKeon is featured in the event discussing marine birds</data>
      <data key="d6">1e20e07194c6b756df1b77ab0d6b272b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POLAR BEARS" target="ROCHESTER AMERICANS">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The Rochester Americans have partnered with Seneca Park Zoo through the Defend the Ice program, which focuses on collaborative efforts to support and promote environmental conservation initiatives.</data>
      <data key="d6">9693c6d355708849ecd97fe93b0cd8f2,f7d18cffd13aa901313d3d4fceef2575</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POLAR BEARS" target="POLAR BEARS INTERNATIONAL">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Conservation efforts supported by this organization</data>
      <data key="d6">f7d18cffd13aa901313d3d4fceef2575</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POLAR BEARS" target="SEA ICE LOSS">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Polar bears are affected by the loss of sea ice, impacting their habitat and food sources</data>
      <data key="d6">14d429568463adbb525417ad6aa15254</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POLAR BEARS" target="SOUTHERN BEAUFORT SEA">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Polar bears historically spend most of their life in this region</data>
      <data key="d6">14d429568463adbb525417ad6aa15254</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POLAR BEARS" target="RINGED SEALS">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Ringed seals are a primary prey for polar bears</data>
      <data key="d6">14d429568463adbb525417ad6aa15254</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POLAR BEARS" target="BEARDED SEALS">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Bearded seals are another primary prey for polar bears</data>
      <data key="d6">14d429568463adbb525417ad6aa15254</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POLAR BEARS" target="WHALE CARCASSES">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Whale carcasses provide a food source for polar bears during periods with little to no sea ice</data>
      <data key="d6">14d429568463adbb525417ad6aa15254</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POLAR BEARS" target="BEAR-HUMAN CONFLICT">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Attraction to human settlements by polar bears creates potential for conflict</data>
      <data key="d6">14d429568463adbb525417ad6aa15254</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POLAR BEARS" target="BOWHEAD WHALES">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Polar bears are attracted to the remains of bowhead whales for food</data>
      <data key="d6">14d429568463adbb525417ad6aa15254</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POLAR BEARS" target="COLLARS">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Collars are used to track the movements and behaviors of polar bears</data>
      <data key="d6">14d429568463adbb525417ad6aa15254</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POLAR BEARS" target="ZOO SETTING">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Studies on polar bears' feeding habits are conducted in a zoo setting</data>
      <data key="d6">14d429568463adbb525417ad6aa15254</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POLAR BEARS" target="WHALE REMAINS">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Whale remains provide a significant food source for polar bears during periods of sea ice loss</data>
      <data key="d6">14d429568463adbb525417ad6aa15254</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POLAR BEARS" target="FEEDING ECOLOGY">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
